    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F (220 degrees C). Pour butter into a 9x13-inch baking dish.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Whisk together egg, milk, and pepper in a shallow dish. Place stuffing mix in a separate shallow dish. Dip pork chops in egg mixture, then coat with stuffing mix.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/0kwF6F43YZOCbb2sfL2L15Tc8ks=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/24681-oven-fried-pork-chop-step2-289-4x3-252a6581e105476791477c2efc45485c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/24681/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lay pork chops in the prepared dish.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/rLT0DvNadj0YAr6k7gVR0h-y0lM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/24681-oven-fried-pork-chop-step3-292-4x3-4a025ddbaa034e7bb88fa9d398446b95.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/24681/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven for 10 minutes. Flip chops and bake until no longer pink in the center and juices run clear, about 10 more minutes. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read at least 145 degrees F (74 degrees C).",
